WEBVTT

00:01:58.930 --> 00:01:59.760
Chief.

00:02:01.890 --> 00:02:04.220
I brought you the report from the third laboratory.

00:02:06.430 --> 00:02:07.430
Chief?

00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:11.270
You should turn the lights on; this isn't good for your eyes.

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:12.060
Ah.

00:02:13.650 --> 00:02:16.360
What are you reading with so much fervor?

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:20.070
That's a special envelope used by military officers...

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:26.750
Let us continue our experiment...

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:29.500
...my sweet boy from 901...

00:02:47.810 --> 00:03:09.540
Kill!
Töten Sie: German for "Kill!"

00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:09.580
Töten Sie: German for "Kill!"

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:26.890
What are you doing, Corporal?

00:03:33.270 --> 00:03:34.190
Let's go!

00:03:35.060 --> 00:03:36.440
Time to do some war relief!

00:04:06.350 --> 00:04:09.310
But man... it's been three years since the war already...

00:04:09.350 --> 00:04:11.270
...and this country is still miserable...

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:12.640
Yeah...

00:04:12.890 --> 00:04:15.350
We got no homes, no jobs...

00:04:15.650 --> 00:04:18.480
At least we could eat and drink for free during the war,

00:04:18.520 --> 00:04:20.230
and the bed was pretty warm, too...

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:24.280
It's so bad right now, I even want to go back to the army.

00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:27.280
Oh, you up, my man?

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:29.330
What's wrong?

00:04:29.910 --> 00:04:32.500
You had another nightmare or something?

00:04:32.540 --> 00:04:34.330
You were mumbling something.

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:42.420
No, today's dream was actually a nice one.

00:04:46.130 --> 00:04:48.100
Viscount Wolkins?

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:51.140
Who was that?

00:04:51.180 --> 00:04:54.060
Huh? We almost got killed by him!

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:56.140
He made us tank targets.

00:04:56.350 --> 00:04:59.520
Oh, yes, yes, I remember.

00:04:59.560 --> 00:05:01.940
That abominable feudal lord.

00:05:01.980 --> 00:05:05.450
Do you only remember women's names or something?

00:05:06.570 --> 00:05:08.780
The problem right now is not the viscount,

00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:10.280
but that tank of his.

00:05:10.330 --> 00:05:12.700
What do you mean, Lieutenant Webner?

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:15.620
The automatic reloading device in the cannon section of the tank...

00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:16.670
That device...

00:05:18.290 --> 00:05:22.000
...even inside the Empire,
is still technology in the developmental stage.

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:26.010
It's not something a rural viscount can obtain easily.

00:05:26.340 --> 00:05:30.010
However, "someone" fully developed that technology.

00:05:31.510 --> 00:05:36.350
I need you guys in the S.S.III to figure out where he got his hands on this.

00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:38.980
Come on, you don't have to get <i>us  to do it.</i>

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:43.030
Why not ask Wolkins himself?

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:45.860
That doesn't seem to be possible.

00:05:46.190 --> 00:05:49.660
He's being treated in the military sanatorium.

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:51.780
I'm a noble...

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:53.700
I'm important...

00:05:53.740 --> 00:05:56.660
I'm the most important noble in this world...

00:05:58.120 --> 00:06:01.170
I don't think he's in any state to tell us anything meaningful.

00:06:03.420 --> 00:06:04.590
And now...

00:06:05.090 --> 00:06:06.630
Here's our call.

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:18.480
Dr. Colt?

00:06:18.770 --> 00:06:20.730
And... who's that?

00:06:20.770 --> 00:06:22.440
For Christ's sake...

00:06:22.690 --> 00:06:25.480
Try to learn some names that don't belong to women already!

00:06:25.860 --> 00:06:27.780
You should've learned this back in the academy, right?

00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:31.910
Dr. Colt, nicknamed the "father of tanks",

00:06:31.950 --> 00:06:34.990
was a very great man who helped contribute to the earliest stage of tank development.

00:06:35.490 --> 00:06:40.040
Dr. Colt should know something about the tank in question.

00:06:40.710 --> 00:06:41.750
What's wrong, Machs?

00:06:42.920 --> 00:06:44.090
N-Nothing.

00:06:49.220 --> 00:06:52.220
"What kind of person is the corporal?"

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:55.260
What kind? Well, he's just a nice guy.

00:06:56.930 --> 00:06:58.640
Tanks are...

00:07:01.270 --> 00:07:03.900
...the strongest weapons on the face of this earth.

00:07:04.900 --> 00:07:07.610
A massive body of ten tons rolling on the ground...

00:07:08.860 --> 00:07:11.150
Tochika: Russian for "pillbox"
...that can even run over a strong tochika.

00:07:11.910 --> 00:07:13.700
Once helpless humans come into their range,

00:07:13.740 --> 00:07:17.120
there's no way for them to have even a chance of survival.

00:07:17.990 --> 00:07:18.910
Yet...

00:07:19.910 --> 00:07:22.040
That corporal, just by himself...

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:26.130
...took care of the tank with just one gun, right?

00:07:27.670 --> 00:07:30.340
Klappe: German for "shutter".
He took one shot at the Klappe,
the part as weak as a kitty's forehead,

00:07:30.380 --> 00:07:33.010
and another shot at the thinly armored tank hatch.

00:07:33.050 --> 00:07:35.640
It's as if he caught on to the tank nicely and took his shot.

00:07:36.510 --> 00:07:38.140
I'll ask you one more time.

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:43.520
What kind of person is Corporal Randel Oland, Machs?

00:07:47.020 --> 00:07:48.190
Sergeant Major.

00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:49.730
Sergeant Major!

00:07:50.740 --> 00:07:51.990
Are you all right?

00:07:52.320 --> 00:07:53.950
You don't look too good.

00:07:53.950 --> 00:07:54.700
Hey!

00:07:54.700 --> 00:07:56.280
Corporal, you're heavy!

00:07:56.280 --> 00:07:57.330
Corporal!

00:08:00.540 --> 00:08:02.710
Nah, it's nothing.

00:08:10.010 --> 00:08:12.800
For a great man, he sure lives in a godforsaken place.

00:08:12.800 --> 00:08:13.380
Shh.

00:08:14.220 --> 00:08:15.470
Dr. Colt?

00:08:15.470 --> 00:08:16.760
Are you there?

00:08:17.010 --> 00:08:20.640
I am 2nd Lieutenant Alice L. Malvin from the State Section.

00:08:23.560 --> 00:08:27.310
Must be a super pig-headed old man, I bet.

00:08:30.320 --> 00:08:32.570
Well, I'm sorry for being pig-headed.

00:08:33.530 --> 00:08:35.240
I'm Colt.

00:08:35.910 --> 00:08:37.370
How may I help you?

00:08:43.960 --> 00:08:49.000
My, it's such an honor to be able to talk to someone featured in textbooks!

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:50.050
No, really!

00:08:50.050 --> 00:08:54.260
I mean, when you hear Dr. Colt,
you think the "father of tanks", right?

00:08:54.260 --> 00:08:56.890
Although our mission doesn't directly involve tanks,

00:08:56.890 --> 00:08:59.430
in order to understand their prowess,

00:08:59.430 --> 00:09:03.180
we need to fully appreciate your greatness, Dr. Colt! Yes, sirree!

00:09:04.770 --> 00:09:09.150
It's a design that didn't even exist back when I was there.

00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:14.150
Such a publication wasn't announced at the Alliance of Western Nations Technological Conference either.

00:09:14.530 --> 00:09:15.530
I see.

00:09:15.990 --> 00:09:21.910
This system is far superior, technologically, to what any country currently possesses.

00:09:23.250 --> 00:09:24.410
What about its analysis?

00:09:24.540 --> 00:09:25.370
Huh?

00:09:25.370 --> 00:09:28.960
How far have you analyzed this tank?

00:09:28.960 --> 00:09:30.880
We've just begun analyzing.

00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:34.970
I see... just begun, eh?

00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:43.850
Unfortunately, I'm unable to give you any more help with just this data.

00:09:43.970 --> 00:09:45.850
Thank you for your help.

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:50.860
What? We're leaving?

00:09:51.230 --> 00:09:53.110
LT? LT!

00:09:58.700 --> 00:10:00.870
T-This gun is...

00:10:06.450 --> 00:10:08.370
T-This gun is...

00:10:08.670 --> 00:10:09.870
...the Corporal's...

00:10:10.540 --> 00:10:12.880
No, wait, Dr. Colt, what is this?

00:10:14.130 --> 00:10:16.670
That's a "door knocker".

00:10:17.010 --> 00:10:18.340
"Door knocker"?

00:10:18.720 --> 00:10:22.390
It's the name of this 13mm anti-tank gun.

00:10:23.220 --> 00:10:26.390
There was an absurd project a long time ago.

00:10:27.020 --> 00:10:30.020
It proposed to increase a foot soldier's firepower to the limit...

00:10:30.020 --> 00:10:33.980
...and make them rival tanks in terms of power.

00:10:34.110 --> 00:10:36.650
A human being... rivaling a tank?

00:10:37.150 --> 00:10:39.450
Yes, absurd, don't you think?

00:10:39.950 --> 00:10:43.740
But in response to the demands of the higher-ups in the military,

00:10:44.120 --> 00:10:47.500
the technicians came up with a last resort idea.

00:10:47.830 --> 00:10:50.750
That idea was to make a large-caliber gun for foot soldiers,

00:10:51.210 --> 00:10:56.130
which is basically this 13mm anti-tank gun
you are looking at right now.

00:10:57.760 --> 00:10:58.970
13mm...

00:10:59.840 --> 00:11:02.800
Its mass, firepower, recoil...

00:11:02.970 --> 00:11:05.430
All the specs asked of this weapon...

00:11:05.430 --> 00:11:08.140
...and the theoretical limits that humans could endure...

00:11:08.390 --> 00:11:13.400
That was this 13mm-caliber the technicians came up with.

00:11:14.110 --> 00:11:15.860
It is powerful,

00:11:16.360 --> 00:11:20.200
but it's not strong enough to stand against the main battle tanks of today.

00:11:20.740 --> 00:11:23.910
If it were to stand against them, there's only one method,

00:11:24.570 --> 00:11:27.660
and that is to press the muzzle of the gun closely to the tank...

00:11:27.660 --> 00:11:29.750
...and shoot at absolute point-blank range.

00:11:30.540 --> 00:11:31.670
Point-blank range?

00:11:38.000 --> 00:11:39.260
Door knocker...

00:11:39.380 --> 00:11:42.090
Well, the project came to a dead end.

00:11:42.550 --> 00:11:45.930
This gun never went into production.

00:11:46.680 --> 00:11:49.600
This is just a mock-up for us to see.

00:11:50.180 --> 00:11:54.690
Besides, in the face of a massive monster like a tank,

00:11:54.940 --> 00:12:00.820
do you think there are any foot soldiers...
any humans willing to pull a suicidal tactic like this?

00:12:07.200 --> 00:12:08.950
Machs, you're late!

00:12:11.620 --> 00:12:12.960
I-I'm sorry!

00:12:21.050 --> 00:12:25.340
Who in the world are you, Corporal Randel Oland?

00:12:27.010 --> 00:12:30.220
Is that lantern from your former unit?

00:12:30.720 --> 00:12:32.640
Ah, what was its name?

00:12:33.890 --> 00:12:37.360
901... Anti-Tank Trooper...

00:12:37.650 --> 00:12:39.320
901?

00:12:39.940 --> 00:12:40.730
9...

00:12:47.870 --> 00:12:48.990
Machs.

00:12:49.950 --> 00:12:51.750
Stop daydreaming.

00:12:52.290 --> 00:12:54.460
We need to head to the development laboratory next.

00:12:54.460 --> 00:12:55.620
Stop wasting time.

00:12:55.620 --> 00:12:56.420
Yes, sir.

00:13:05.470 --> 00:13:07.050
Yes, that's right.

00:13:07.800 --> 00:13:10.390
It's <i>that  tank indeed.</i>

00:13:11.600 --> 00:13:14.140
Yes, carry out your job in its entirety.

00:13:28.070 --> 00:13:29.070
Yeah?

00:13:29.490 --> 00:13:31.830
So, no clues in the end?

00:13:36.250 --> 00:13:39.580
Sorry for having you come all the way down here to report.

00:13:39.580 --> 00:13:41.290
No, this is part of our mission.

00:13:41.920 --> 00:13:45.590
That means we have no choice but to dismantle it.

00:13:46.050 --> 00:13:48.890
Hey, get the bar and burner ready!

00:13:48.890 --> 00:13:50.350
We're going to strip off the armor!

00:13:50.350 --> 00:13:51.760
All right!!!

00:13:51.760 --> 00:13:53.010
Okay!

00:13:53.010 --> 00:13:55.520
You seem to be having fun.

00:13:57.560 --> 00:13:59.480
Dismantle it and rebuild it.

00:13:59.480 --> 00:14:01.690
Then, dismantle and rebuild it again.

00:14:01.690 --> 00:14:04.190
That's the real fun in being a technician.

00:14:04.440 --> 00:14:06.360
You make it sound like playing a game.

00:14:06.530 --> 00:14:08.660
Stop saying unnecessary things!

00:14:09.240 --> 00:14:10.780
Sorry... hmm?

00:14:11.950 --> 00:14:14.990
Anesan... what's that tough-looking vehicle there?

00:14:15.620 --> 00:14:16.620
Ahh, that.

00:14:16.620 --> 00:14:20.290
That's a new-model armored car that will be used by Section I.

00:14:20.630 --> 00:14:23.250
Hmm, aren't Section I people lucky?

00:14:23.250 --> 00:14:25.550
I mean, compared to us Section III people...

00:14:25.550 --> 00:14:27.170
What are you talking about?

00:14:27.170 --> 00:14:29.260
We gave you a new train last time!

00:14:29.260 --> 00:14:31.850
That was just a big drill, man!

00:14:35.100 --> 00:14:36.850
Hey, the cannon's...

00:14:37.100 --> 00:14:38.350
Is someone test driving it?

00:14:51.490 --> 00:14:53.160
What... the... hell...

00:14:54.830 --> 00:14:56.040
Sound the alarms!

00:14:56.040 --> 00:14:57.160
Contact HQ!

00:14:57.160 --> 00:14:58.540
We have a C-34 here!

00:15:03.250 --> 00:15:04.960
Smoke discharger?!

00:15:04.960 --> 00:15:06.000
Chief!

00:15:06.250 --> 00:15:07.340
What's going on?!

00:15:09.800 --> 00:15:11.760
Damn it! Tear-gas grenades?

00:15:11.760 --> 00:15:13.260
What are they trying to do?

00:15:18.430 --> 00:15:20.060
Who are they?

00:15:20.850 --> 00:15:23.770
Wait... are they trying to destroy the tank?

00:15:24.110 --> 00:15:24.940
Chief!

00:15:24.940 --> 00:15:26.230
I know!

00:15:26.230 --> 00:15:28.070
I don't know who they are,

00:15:28.070 --> 00:15:29.940
but their target is that tank!

00:15:29.940 --> 00:15:31.820
We can't take them on by ourselves.

00:15:31.820 --> 00:15:33.240
Call for reinforcements right now!

00:15:33.820 --> 00:15:35.950
Sorry, the gas is making my eyes...

00:15:35.950 --> 00:15:36.870
Fool!

00:15:36.870 --> 00:15:38.580
This gas will disperse right away!

00:15:38.580 --> 00:15:39.580
Calm down!

00:15:39.580 --> 00:15:41.830
Don't worsen the situation with your confusion!

00:15:46.750 --> 00:15:47.800
It's coming out?

00:15:48.130 --> 00:15:49.380
What's it trying to do?

00:15:51.510 --> 00:15:53.720
Those are blitz-purpose Hedgerow Cutters!

00:15:55.430 --> 00:15:57.180
They're planning to completely destroy it?

00:15:58.260 --> 00:15:59.220
Machs!

00:16:02.940 --> 00:16:03.730
Machs!

00:16:04.100 --> 00:16:05.860
Get up! Run away!

00:16:10.610 --> 00:16:13.150
Machs! Run!

00:16:32.420 --> 00:16:33.420
Corporal...

00:16:49.770 --> 00:16:51.530
Huh, that's weird...

00:16:51.900 --> 00:16:54.820
Why aren't I thinking "thank you"...

00:16:55.660 --> 00:16:57.030
...or "are you okay"...

00:16:59.160 --> 00:17:01.240
...but "you monster" instead...

00:17:21.680 --> 00:17:22.720
I see...

00:17:23.810 --> 00:17:24.680
This is...

00:17:25.600 --> 00:17:28.560
This is... point-blank...

00:17:36.530 --> 00:17:37.780
This is the killzone...

00:17:37.990 --> 00:17:39.620
...the world the corporal lives in...

00:17:40.580 --> 00:17:41.950
I can't breathe!

00:17:42.120 --> 00:17:43.870
My stomach's turning inside out...

00:17:45.870 --> 00:17:48.460
I'm scared... I'm scared...

00:17:49.040 --> 00:17:49.960
I'm scared...

00:17:52.000 --> 00:17:54.880
but the thing I'm scared of the most is...

00:17:55.760 --> 00:17:59.800
Töten Sie...

00:17:59.800 --> 00:18:03.890
Kill...
Töten Sie...

00:18:03.890 --> 00:18:07.730
Kill...

00:18:27.580 --> 00:18:31.000
All three suspects that stole the armored car are dead.

00:18:31.250 --> 00:18:33.000
They were all pronounced dead on the spot.

00:18:33.290 --> 00:18:36.960
Additionally, there were no belongings that could indicate their identities.

00:18:37.380 --> 00:18:41.140
Their objective was the preservation of the tank's secret, eh?

00:18:41.140 --> 00:18:44.470
Yes, technical recovery is no longer feasible.

00:18:46.810 --> 00:18:47.980
And the corporal?

00:18:51.100 --> 00:18:52.650
He suffered injuries,

00:18:52.770 --> 00:18:54.730
but fortunately, none were to the bone.

00:18:54.980 --> 00:18:57.190
He can be discharged from the hospital in one month.

00:19:02.870 --> 00:19:03.990
I see.

00:19:04.530 --> 00:19:05.990
Thanks for the report.

00:19:06.660 --> 00:19:09.210
Your injuries weren't light either, right?

00:19:09.660 --> 00:19:12.000
Go to the hospital and visit the corporal-

00:19:12.000 --> 00:19:12.790
Captain Hunks!
Go to the hospital and visit the corporal-

00:19:12.790 --> 00:19:13.040
Captain Hunks!

00:19:14.040 --> 00:19:18.050
What exactly is 901 Anti-Tank Trooper?

00:19:19.510 --> 00:19:21.590
What are you asking all of a sudden?

00:19:22.220 --> 00:19:27.390
That's the unit the corporal belonged in a long time ago.

00:19:27.680 --> 00:19:29.850
I should've noticed this earlier.

00:19:30.520 --> 00:19:34.730
September 9th is the day
the first Emperor died on the battlefield.

00:19:35.020 --> 00:19:38.860
It was treated as a taboo number afterwards,

00:19:38.860 --> 00:19:41.070
and it's an unwritten rule never to use the number 9 in the army, right?

00:19:44.030 --> 00:19:46.620
That's a very old convention, though.

00:19:47.200 --> 00:19:50.080
It's being used a lot lately.

00:19:50.080 --> 00:19:53.920
Even so, I don't think it's ever been used in front of a unit name!

00:19:55.920 --> 00:19:58.670
This is the complete book that contains all
the military units during the Imperial years.

00:19:59.590 --> 00:20:04.180
There is not a single record of any unit having the 900 series as their unit designation!

00:20:04.510 --> 00:20:08.890
A unit known as 901-ATT in our army does not exist!

00:20:12.980 --> 00:20:15.400
Non-existent, eh?

00:20:15.610 --> 00:20:17.110
Very well put.

00:20:17.690 --> 00:20:20.190
That's why they were called...

00:20:20.570 --> 00:20:22.110
..."Invisible 9"...

00:20:22.320 --> 00:20:25.070
Invisible... 9...

00:20:26.620 --> 00:20:28.200
Th-That's...

00:20:29.490 --> 00:20:30.660
Captain Hunks!

00:20:30.660 --> 00:20:31.540
Something happened!

00:20:31.540 --> 00:20:32.210
What?

00:20:35.040 --> 00:20:35.920
Well...

00:20:35.920 --> 00:20:39.250
Viscount Wolkins committed suicide inside the sanatorium!

00:20:40.590 --> 00:20:41.510
That's...

00:20:42.420 --> 00:20:43.470
No way...

00:20:44.970 --> 00:20:47.510
To keep his mouth shut about the tank, huh?

00:20:49.350 --> 00:20:51.390
I don't know which organization did this,

00:20:51.390 --> 00:20:53.520
but they're doing a thorough job all right.

00:20:54.140 --> 00:21:01.570
In this world, there is information that could get you killed just for "knowing".

00:21:02.400 --> 00:21:06.240
Invisible 9 might be that type of information, too...

00:21:07.820 --> 00:21:11.370
Do you want to stick your head into it even so?

00:21:11.370 --> 00:21:12.700
Sergeant Major Machs!

00:21:15.410 --> 00:21:16.250
Yes, sir.

00:21:31.010 --> 00:21:32.010
Corporal...

00:21:41.110 --> 00:21:42.190
Here...

00:21:42.190 --> 00:21:44.190
I got some hospital food today.

00:21:44.440 --> 00:21:45.650
Looks tasty, right?

00:21:46.990 --> 00:21:48.160
What's the matter?

00:21:48.160 --> 00:21:50.620
You guys always come over and gobble it up...

00:21:52.120 --> 00:21:53.290
I see...

00:21:54.120 --> 00:21:57.960
...it's because I've got the smell of blood on me...

00:23:30.930 --> 00:23:31.760
Mer-kun,

00:23:31.760 --> 00:23:34.300
it's kind of lonely now that the corporal is in the hospital.

00:23:34.300 --> 00:23:36.810
The scenery of Section III looks all different now.

00:23:37.140 --> 00:23:39.180
By the way, who's this nurse?

00:23:39.600 --> 00:23:41.810
Next time, "The Shallow-Brained Men".

00:23:41.810 --> 00:23:43.900
Come get us if you're not scared!
